1.     Definitions

       In these Conditions:

       "Agency and Accounts Agreement" means an agency and accounts agreement dated the
       Signing Date between the Issuer, the Agent Bank, the Computation Agent, the Italian Paying
       Agent, the Principal Paying Agent, the Listing and Luxembourg Paying Agent, the
       Transaction Bank, the Swap Counterparty and the Representative of the Noteholders;

       "Auditing Agreement" means the auditing agreement dated the Signing Date between the
       Issuer, the Representative of the Noteholders and the Auditors;

       "Auditors" means PKF Italia S.p.A. with offices at Viale Vittorio Veneto, 10, I-20124,
       Milan, Italy, and includes any successor firm of auditors appointed from time to time by the
       Issuer;

       "Banking Act" means the Italian legislative decree No. 385 of 1 September 1993;

       "Business Day" means a day on which banks are open for business in Milan, Luxembourg
       and London and which is a TARGET Settlement Day;

       "Calculation Date" means the second Business Day preceding each Interest Payment Date,
       the first Calculation Date being on 25 June 2007;

       "Cancellation Date" means the earlier of (i) the date on which the Notes are redeemed in full
       and (ii) the last Business Day in December 2026;

       "Certification Process" means the process of certification under which the Health
       Authorities validated the Claims, to be covered by the Settlement Agreements and the
       Delegations of Payment;

       "Clearstream, Luxembourg" means Clearstream Banking, société anonyme;

       "Collateral Account Bank" means any depository institution located in England and
